  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Boundary Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The Boundary Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Validate at the edge",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Check ==every byte from outside== once, at the edge",
                "Inputs: body, query, path, headers, cookies, uploads",
                "Runs {green:before} business logic",
                "**Parse, don't validate**: raw input → ==typed object==",
                "Code past the edge never re-checks"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Layers: earliest failure wins",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Syntax",
                    "sub": "JSON parses",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Schema",
                    "sub": "types, required, formats",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Authz",
                    "sub": "may this caller?",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Semantics",
                    "sub": "end date after start",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Fail at the earliest layer**",
                "Authz before rules: a state check must not answer an unauthorized caller"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. The server decides",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Client checks are ==UX only==; curl and scripts skip the UI",
                "Server must validate everything"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why at the edge?** One enforcement point; services trust typed data",
                "**Parse, don't validate?** Return a typed object, not a yes/no",
                "**Client checks enough?** No, requests bypass the UI",
                "**Schema vs logic?** Schema: shape. Logic: rules needing state"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Validate once at the edge; trust the types after."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Schemas: Declarative Validation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Schemas: Declarative Validation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Contract",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Declare ==type, required, min/max, regex, enum, nested== once",
                "A library enforces it: Pydantic, Zod, Joi, JSON Schema, Bean Validation"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Unknown Fields, Input Models",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Reject unknown fields==: `.strict()` or `additionalProperties:false`",
                "Catches typos and ==mass assignment== (overposting)",
                "{green:Allowlist} fields, never blocklist",
                "Separate input schema from DB model: clients cannot set `id` or `role`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "CreateUser (input)",
                "User (DB)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "id",
                  "no",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "role",
                  "no",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "email",
                  "yes",
                  "yes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: Zod",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`safeParse` never throws: returns ==success== with data, or a list of ==issues=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const Create = z.object({",
                "  email: z.string().email(),",
                "  age: z.number().int().min(18),",
                "}).strict();",
                "const r = Create.safeParse(body);",
                "// r.success ? r.data : r.error.issues"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why schema over if-checks?** One declared contract, reused, no gaps",
                "**Mass assignment?** Client sets fields like `role`; input model plus strict blocks it",
                "**Unknown fields?** Strict rejects them; lenient silently drops them",
                "**Coercion?** Once, in the schema at the edge ('5' to 5)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "400 vs 422 and Status Codes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "400 vs 422 and Status Codes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. 400 vs 422",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Request",
                "Code",
                "Why"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Broken JSON, bad query syntax",
                  "==400==",
                  "Cannot be parsed"
                ],
                [
                  "Valid JSON, `age: -1`",
                  "==422==",
                  "Parsed, fails rules"
                ],
                [
                  "Valid JSON, bad email format",
                  "==422==",
                  "Schema or semantic fail"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:FastAPI}: 422 for schema errors",
                "{blue:Spring, Express}: often 400 for both",
                "==Pick one convention== and document it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Related Codes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Code",
                "Use when"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "401",
                  "Not authenticated"
                ],
                [
                  "403",
                  "Authenticated, not allowed"
                ],
                [
                  "404",
                  "Resource missing"
                ],
                [
                  "==409==",
                  "State conflict, e.g. duplicate email"
                ],
                [
                  "413",
                  "Body too large"
                ],
                [
                  "415",
                  "Unsupported Content-Type"
                ],
                [
                  "429",
                  "Rate limited"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Avoid",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Validation failure as `200` with an error body: use 422 or 400",
                "Bad client input as `500`: it is a 4xx, never 5xx"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "409 vs 422",
              "text": "Value is invalid by itself: ==422==. Value is fine but clashes with existing state: ==409==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Consistent Error Bodies and Field-Level Errors",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Consistent Error Bodies and Field-Level Errors",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. One Envelope",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One ==envelope== for every error: RFC 9457 **Problem Details**",
                "Fields: `type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`",
                "Content-Type: `application/problem+json`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Field-Level Errors",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Add an `errors` array of `field`, `code`, `message` so clients can highlight each input",
                "Return ==all== errors in one response: one round trip",
                "Nested and array paths: `address.zip`, `items[0].qty`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "json",
              "lines": [
                "{\"title\":\"Invalid input\",\"status\":422,\"errors\":[",
                "{\"field\":\"address.zip\",\"code\":\"invalid_format\"},",
                "{\"field\":\"name\",\"code\":\"required\"}",
                "]}"
              ],
              "note": "Problem Details plus errors[]"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Codes vs Messages",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "code",
                "message"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Reader",
                  "Client code",
                  "Human"
                ],
                [
                  "Stability",
                  "**Stable**, never renamed",
                  "May change or be translated"
                ],
                [
                  "Example",
                  "`too_short`, `required`",
                  "Name is required"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Branching on message text",
                "Stack traces, SQL or secrets in the error body"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Clients branch on ==code==, never on message. Same shape on every endpoint."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sanitization and Size Limits",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Sanitization and Size Limits",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Validate vs Sanitize",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Validation",
                "Sanitization"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Action",
                  "{red:Rejects} bad input",
                  "{orange:Changes} the input"
                ],
                [
                  "Examples",
                  "422 on bad email",
                  "trim, normalize Unicode, strip control chars"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Prefer ==rejecting== over silently altering data",
                "Silent edits hide client bugs and surprise users"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sanitize by Output Context",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Output",
                "Defence"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "SQL",
                  "==parameterized queries=="
                ],
                [
                  "HTML",
                  "escape on render"
                ],
                [
                  "Shell",
                  "no string concatenation; pass an arg list"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Escape on ==output==: the right escape depends on the destination",
                "Input cleaning alone does {red:not} stop injection"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Size Limits",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Limit every level: ==body bytes== (**413**), string length, array length, nesting depth, upload size",
                "Enforce at the proxy or server, before the body is fully read",
                "Also bound: pagination (==max limit=100==), number ranges, regex (ReDoS), decompressed size (zip bombs)"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No limits = DoS",
              "text": "One huge body, deep nesting, a ReDoS regex or a zip bomb can exhaust ==CPU or memory== of the server."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Validation Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Validation Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Order of Checks",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Limits",
                    "sub": "413 · 415",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Authn",
                    "sub": "401",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Parse",
                    "sub": "400",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Schema",
                    "sub": "422",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Authz",
                    "sub": "403",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rules",
                    "sub": "422 · 409",
                    "ink": "pink"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Validate outside data ==once at the edge==; trust typed data after",
                "==Authz before rules==: a duplicate check must not answer a caller without permission"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Codes and Error Body",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Code",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`400`",
                  "malformed"
                ],
                [
                  "`422`",
                  "semantically invalid"
                ],
                [
                  "`409`",
                  "conflict"
                ],
                [
                  "`413`",
                  "too large"
                ],
                [
                  "`415`",
                  "wrong media type"
                ],
                [
                  "`429`",
                  "rate limited"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Problem Details plus `errors[]`: same shape everywhere, ==all errors at once=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "json",
              "lines": [
                "{\"type\": \"/errors/validation\", \"title\": \"Invalid\",",
                "\"status\": 422, \"detail\": \"1 field failed\",",
                "\"errors\": [{\"field\": \"age\",",
                "\"code\": \"too_small\", \"message\": \"Min 18\"}]}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Schemas",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Allowlist== fields",
                "Strict: reject unknown keys",
                "Separate input and DB models",
                "No client-set `id` or `role`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Bad POST path?** limits 413/415 → 401 → parse 400 → schema 422 → 403 → rules 422/409 → error body",
                "**Same shape across services?** One shared Problem Details schema with stable codes"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An API follows the 400/422 split. Which status for `{\"age\": -1}`, and which for `{\"age\": `?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`{\"age\": -1}` parses fine but breaks a rule: **422**.",
                "`{\"age\": ` is broken JSON: **400**."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A handler checks for a duplicate email and returns 409 before checking permissions. What is wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It tells a caller with no permission which emails exist.",
                "Order should be parse, schema, authz, then business rules."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`db.save(User(**body))` is called on the raw request body. A client sends `{\"role\":\"admin\"}`. What happens?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Mass assignment: the client sets a field it should not control.",
                "Fix: a strict input schema with allowlisted fields and no `role`."
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "CreateUser = z.object({ email: z.string().email() }).strict()"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}